      "text": "Let's solve step by step.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Simplify the first equation**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\[\n3^a = 81^{b+2}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(81 = 3^4\\), we can write:\n\n\\[\n3^a = (3^4)^{b+2} = 3^{4(b+2)}\n\\]\n\nEquating exponents:\n\n\\[\na = 4(b+2)\n\\]\n\\[\na = 4b + 8\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Simplify the second equation**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\[\n125^b = 5^{a-3}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(125 = 5^3\\), we can write:\n\n\\[\n(5^3)^b = 5^{a-3}\n\\]\n\\[\n5^{3b} = 5^{a-3}\n\\]\n\nEquating exponents:\n\n\\[\n3b = a - 3\n\\]\n\\[\na = 3b + 3\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Solve the system**\n\nFrom Step 1: \\(a = 4b + 8\\)  \nFrom Step 2: \\(a = 3b + 3\\)\n\nSet them equal:\n\n\\[\n4b + 8 = 3b + 3\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -5\n\\]\n\nThen:\n\n\\[\na = 3(-5) + 3 = -15 + 3 = -12\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Find \\(ab\\)**\n\n\\[\nab = (-12)(-5) = 60\n\\]\n\n---\n\nThe answer is 60.",
